1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,800
AI agents consume untrusted data from documents, APIs, and voice.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Without an external gateway, prompt injections hijack reasoning before execution begins.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:18,500
ContextShield is a low-latency security gateway positioned in front of the agent.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:26,500
Inbound context is scanned by deterministic rules and Moss semantic retrieval over enterprise policies.

5
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:33,000
Clear threats and safe inputs resolve immediately, while Gemini is gated behind the deterministic path for ambiguous cases.

6
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,500
Downstream agents are strictly isolated from unapproved context.

7
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:54,500
Here is our production proof. An inbound document delivers an instruction override seeking API keys.

8
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,500
ContextShield detects the threat and issues a BLOCK.

9
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:04,500
The protected agent was never called and received no context from the blocked request.

10
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,000
Zero toxic tokens reach the model.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,800
When an isolated malicious instruction is embedded in legitimate documentation, ContextShield sanitizes it.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,300
The hostile override is excised, the payload is revalidated, and only cleaned context reaches the agent.

13
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:41,200
In the audit drawer, we inspect the decision evidence: deterministic rule triggers, observed processing latency, and semantic policy candidates retrieved by Moss.

14
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:49,500
The same boundary protects voice: LiveKit transcribes speech, and ContextShield blocks unsafe context before reaching the agent.

15
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:53,900
ContextShield: inspect first, trust second.
